{
 "id": "saul-family",
 "title": "The Family of Saul",
 "ref": "1 Samuel 14:49–51; 1 Chronicles 8:29–40; 9:35–44",
 "compact": true,
 "col": "plum",
 "intro": [
  "Israel's first king came from Gibeon's leading family of Benjamin. 1 Samuel names Saul's household; Chronicles gives the line twice, before and after the list of Jerusalem's settlers, and carries it about twelve generations past Jonathan, through Mephibosheth (Merib-baal), to the time of the exile.",
  "Chronicles keeps the older names with \"Baal\" (Esh-baal, Merib-baal), which 2 Samuel changes to <i>-bosheth</i>, \"shame.\""
 ],
 "sources": "Hebrew names: Miqra according to the Masorah. Babylonian Talmud, Yoma 22b and Sanhedrin 21a; Rashi on 1 Samuel 14 and 2 Samuel 21. Scholarly summary after the standard commentaries.",
 "anchor": {
  "book": "1CH",
  "c": 8,
  "v": 29
 },
